WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.567
A bright little boy grew up in the countryside of Korea in the mid-1500s.

2
00:00:05.568 --> 00:00:07.970
His name was Yi Sunshin.

3
00:00:07.971 --> 00:00:11.865
Sunshin dreamed of becoming a famous military official.

4
00:00:11.866 --> 00:00:18.350
He often said to himself, "I'm going to be the best military official of my generation.

5
00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:24.036
I will dedicate my life to my country."

6
00:00:24.037 --> 00:00:28.492
It took time for Yi Sunshin to accomplish his dream.

7
00:00:28.493 --> 00:00:33.641
When he was 28 years old, he took the military service examination.

8
00:00:33.642 --> 00:00:38.690
But during the exam, he fell from his horse and broke his leg.

9
00:00:38.691 --> 00:00:48.459
Determined to succeed, Yi Sunshin took the exam again when he was 32 years old, and this time, he passed.

10
00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.683
His military career had finally begun.

11
00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:55.892
From that moment, Yi Sunshin would live his dream.

12
00:00:55.893 --> 00:01:06.944
In 1591, 47-year-old Yi Sunshin became the naval commander in charge of protecting the coast of the Jeolla province of Korea.

13
00:01:06.945 --> 00:01:15.742
This assignment was important because the province is close to Japan, and at that time, Japan and Korea were not on good terms.

14
00:01:15.743 --> 00:01:22.523
Japan had a new ruler, Toyotomi Hideyoshi, and he wanted to take over Korea.

15
00:01:22.524 --> 00:01:29.151
Yi Sunshin knew that Japan might attack Korea at any moment, so he decided to do something about it.

16
00:01:29.152 --> 00:01:33.316
He gathered all his soldiers together for a meeting.

17
00:01:33.317 --> 00:01:36.491
"Listen up, everyone. Korea is in danger.

18
00:01:36.492 --> 00:01:39.128
Japan might attack us at any moment.

19
00:01:39.129 --> 00:01:44.667
We must be prepared. We must begin training," Yi Sunshin said.

20
00:01:44.668 --> 00:01:50.511
Yi Sunshin trained his soldiers daily, but he knew that this preparation would not be enough.

21
00:01:50.512 --> 00:01:54.436
What more could he do?

22
00:01:54.437 --> 00:01:59.132
At night, Yi Sunshin read history books, looking for an answer.

23
00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:03.239
Finally, he read about a ship that was built in 1413.

24
00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:13.661
"Yes, yes, that was a good battleship, sturdy and strong— but not good enough," Yi Sunshin thought.

25
00:02:13.662 --> 00:02:17.236
He scratched his head and thought some more, "That's it!

26
00:02:17.237 --> 00:02:21.130
I'll adapt it and make it into a more powerful ship."

27
00:02:21.131 --> 00:02:28.539
Excited, he pulled out his pen and paper and began to draw his new ship.

28
00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:34.092
Yi Sunshin and his soldiers built many ships before they finally made the perfect new ship.

29
00:02:34.093 --> 00:02:37.993
Everyone celebrated when the hard work was finally over.

30
00:02:37.994 --> 00:02:42.942
They called the final creation "the turtle ship."

31
00:02:42.943 --> 00:02:45.663
The turtle ship was very intimidating.

32
00:02:45.664 --> 00:02:49.445
It had a dragon's head at the front and a turtle's body.

33
00:02:49.446 --> 00:02:55.970
The dragon's head could spit out smoke to hide the ship from the enemy and to confuse them.

34
00:02:55.971 --> 00:03:01.167
The turtle's body was a shell of iron plates that covered the top of the ship.

35
00:03:01.168 --> 00:03:06.449
The shell had sharp iron spikes that would stab attackers if they tried to board.

36
00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:12.783
The iron covering made the turtle ship the world's first ironclad ship.

37
00:03:12.784 --> 00:03:20.555
Yi Sunshin also created holes in the sides of the ship so that his soldiers could look outside and fire the ship's cannons.

38
00:03:20.556 --> 00:03:28.745
The holes were designed so that his soldiers could see the enemy but the enemy could not look inside the ship and see the soldiers.

39
00:03:28.746 --> 00:03:35.852
Yi Sunshin and his soldiers had built a powerful weapon that they knew would help them win many strategic battles.

40
00:03:35.853 --> 00:03:40.379
Yi Sunshin and his soldiers finished the turtle ship just in time.

41
00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:46.341
In April 1592, Japan attacked Korea.

42
00:03:46.342 --> 00:03:50.495
Sunshin and his great turtle ship won their first battle in May.

43
00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:56.160
He and his soldiers fought Japan until the end of the war and won many important battles.

44
00:03:56.161 --> 00:04:08.821
More turtle ships were built, and with these powerful weapons, Sunshin defeated 359 Japanese battleships in four battles in 1592.

45
00:04:08.822 --> 00:04:13.852
During the entire war, he sunk about 700 Japanese battleships.

46
00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:19.323
His victories helped Korea defeat Japan, and he and his ships became famous.

47
00:04:19.324 --> 00:04:26.305
Throughout his life, Yi Sunshin suffered many hardships, but his loyalty to his country never wavered.

48
00:04:26.306 --> 00:04:30.014
His many victories earned him everyone's respect.

49
00:04:30.015 --> 00:04:39.159
On November 19, 1598, Yi Sunshin died bravely in the Battle of Noryang, which ended the Seven Year War with Japan.

50
00:04:39.160 --> 00:04:48.320
To this day, the people of Korea admire Admiral Yi Sunshin as a great hero who gave his life for his people and country.

